---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../consts';

const CALENDLY_URL = 'https://calendly.com/shashank19/15min';
const WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY = 'd165756b-c4fc-484f-9914-97af89d0421e';

const structuredData = [
	{
		'@context': 'https://schema.org',
		'@type': 'Service',
		provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE_TITLE },
		areaServed: 'Worldwide',
		serviceType: 'AI SEO for Restaurants',
		description:
			'AI SEO services for independent restaurants, restaurant groups, and hospitality brands that need visibility in Google, AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity, and other AI search environments.',
	},
	{
		'@context': 'https://schema.org',
		'@type': 'FAQPage',
		mainEntity: [
			{
				'@type': 'Question',
				name: 'How much does SEO cost for restaurants?',
				acceptedAnswer: {
					'@type': 'Answer',
					text: 'Restaurant SEO typically ranges from $1,000 to $5,000 per month depending on the number of locations, market size, and goals. Single-location independents need less than multi-location groups. Many restaurants get significant lift from Google Business Profile optimization and review systems alone, before any content work.',
				},
			},
			{
				'@type': 'Question',
				name: 'How long does restaurant SEO take to work?',
				acceptedAnswer: {
					'@type': 'Answer',
					text: 'Restaurants often see results faster than most local businesses, sometimes within four to eight weeks. The reason is that Google Business Profile fixes, menu schema, and review velocity push results quickly. Brand and category searches like "best Italian restaurant in Brooklyn" take longer in competitive metros.',
				},
			},
			{
				'@type': 'Question',
				name: 'Do restaurants need AI SEO?',
				acceptedAnswer: {
					'@type': 'Answer',
					text: 'Yes. Diners now ask ChatGPT and Perplexity for restaurant recommendations, dietary-restriction-friendly spots, and birthday-worthy patios. Google AI Overviews summarize "best brunch in Austin" instantly. If your restaurant is not surfaced in those AI answers, you lose covers to restaurants that are.',
				},
			},
			{
				'@type': 'Question',
				name: 'What is menu schema and does it matter?',
				acceptedAnswer: {
					'@type': 'Answer',
					text: 'Menu schema (Schema.org Menu) is structured data that tells search engines exactly what dishes you serve, with prices, allergen information, and dietary tags. Properly marked-up menus appear in rich results, get pulled into AI-generated recommendations, and are favored by both Google and AI systems when answering food queries.',
				},
			},
			{
				'@type': 'Question',
				name: 'How important are reviews for restaurant SEO?',
				acceptedAnswer: {
					'@type': 'Answer',
					text: 'Reviews are arguably more important for restaurants than any other vertical. They drive Google Business Profile prominence, feed AI recommendation engines, influence map pack rankings, and shape brand trust. Recent positive reviews matter more than older ones, so review velocity and freshness are now ranking factors in their own right.',
				},
			},
		],
	},
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`AI SEO for Restaurants and Restaurant Groups | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Restaurant SEO and AI search visibility. Win Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT recommendations, and the local map pack for dining queries."
			structuredData={structuredData}
		/>
		<style>
			.svc-page { width: min(1080px, calc(100% - 2rem)); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-9); }

			.svc-hero { padding: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-8); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(0, 0.95fr); gap: var(--space-7); align-items: end; }
			.svc-kicker { display: inline-flex; padding: 0; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; }
			.svc-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4.6vw, 4rem); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.03em; font-weight: 600; margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; max-width: 16ch; }
			.svc-hero-lede p { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(var(--ink), 0.78); max-width: var(--measure); margin: 0; }

			.svc-cta-row { display: flex; gap: var(--space-3); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--space-5); }
			.svc-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; text-decoration: none; }
			.svc-btn-primary { background: rgb(var(--ink)); color: rgb(var(--paper)); }
			.svc-btn-primary:hover { background: var(--signal-deep); }
			.svc-btn-secondary { background: transparent; color: rgb(var(--ink)); border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
			.svc-btn-secondary:hover { border-color: rgb(var(--ink)); }

			.svc-section { padding: var(--space-8) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
			.svc-section h2 { font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 3vw, 2.6rem); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.024em; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); max-width: 18ch; }
			.svc-section > p { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; color: rgba(var(--ink), 0.82); max-width: var(--measure); margin: 0 0 var(--space-6); }

			.svc-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
			.svc-list li { margin: 0; }
			.svc-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 9rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-6); align-items: baseline; padding: var(--space-5) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
			.svc-list li:last-child .svc-row { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
			.svc-row-num { font-family: 'Figtree', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
			.svc-row h3 { font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); letter-spacing: -0.018em; font-weight: 600; }
			.svc-row p { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-muted); margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); max-width: 52ch; }
			.svc-row ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-3); }
			.svc-row ul li { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
			.svc-row ul li + li::before { content: '·'; margin-right: var(--space-3); color: var(--line-strong); }

			.outcomes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-7); margin: var(--space-5) 0 0; }
			.outcome { padding-top: var(--space-4); border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
			.outcome strong { display: block; font-family: 'Figtree', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.15rem; color: rgb(var(--ink)); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
			.outcome span { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-muted); line-height: 1.55; }

			.contact-block { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-7); margin: var(--space-5) 0 0; align-items: start; }
			@media (max-width: 860px) { .svc-hero, .outcomes, .contact-block { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .svc-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); } }

			.contact-card { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: rgb(var(--paper-strong)); }
			.contact-card h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); letter-spacing: -0.015em; font-weight: 600; }
			.contact-card > p { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-muted); margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); }
			.contact-form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); }
			.contact-form label { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: rgba(var(--ink), 0.85); text-transform: uppercase; }
			.contact-form .req { color: var(--signal-deep); margin-left: 0.15rem; }
			.contact-form input:focus-visible, .contact-form select:focus-visible, .contact-form textarea:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--signal); outline-offset: 1px; border-color: rgb(var(--ink)); }
			.contact-form input, .contact-form select, .contact-form textarea { width: 100%; padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: 0.95rem; font-family: inherit; background: rgb(var(--paper)); color: rgb(var(--ink)); box-sizing: border-box; }
			.contact-form textarea { min-height: 120px; resize: vertical; }
			.contact-form button { margin-top: var(--space-3); padding: 0.85rem 1rem; background: rgb(var(--ink)); color: rgb(var(--paper)); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; border: none; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); cursor: pointer; }
			.contact-form button:hover { background: var(--signal-deep); }
			.form-status { margin-top: var(--space-3); font-size: 0.9rem; display: none; }
			.form-status.success { display: block; color: #047857; }
			.form-status.error { display: block; color: #b91c1c; }

			.faq-list { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
			.faq-list li { padding: var(--space-5) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
			.faq-list li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
			.faq-list h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); letter-spacing: -0.012em; font-weight: 600; }
			.faq-list p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 56ch; }

			.svc-figure { margin: var(--space-6) 0 0; padding: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: rgb(var(--paper-strong)); overflow: hidden; }
			.svc-figure svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
			.svc-figure figcaption { padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.55; font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-muted); }
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main id="main-content" class="svc-page">
			<section class="svc-hero">
				<div>
					<span class="svc-kicker">AI SEO for Restaurants</span>
					<h1>AI SEO for Restaurants and Restaurant Groups</h1>
				</div>
				<div class="svc-hero-lede">
					<p>
						Diners no longer browse Yelp lists. They ask ChatGPT for a "romantic spot for an anniversary
						in Brooklyn." They ask Perplexity which spots are open late with vegan options. Google AI
						Overviews summarize "best brunch near me" without sending a single click to your site. The
						restaurants cited in those answers fill tables. The ones that are not, do not.
					</p>
					<div class="svc-cta-row">
						<a class="svc-btn svc-btn-primary" href={CALENDLY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a 15-min call &rarr;</a>
						<a class="svc-btn svc-btn-secondary" href="#quote">Request a quote</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<figure class="svc-figure" aria-labelledby="svc-figure-caption">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 1080 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="How restaurants get cited by AI: Google Business Profile, Menu schema with dietary tags, atmosphere content, and recent reviews flow into a cited restaurant recommendation">
					<rect width="1080" height="360" fill="rgb(246,245,240)" />
					<g stroke="rgb(14,17,22)" stroke-opacity="0.06"><line x1="0" y1="48" x2="1080" y2="48" /><line x1="0" y1="312" x2="1080" y2="312" /></g>
					<text x="48" y="32" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" letter-spacing="3" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" fill-opacity="0.6">INPUT SIGNALS</text>
					<text x="540" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" letter-spacing="3" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" fill-opacity="0.6">AI SYNTHESIS</text>
					<text x="1032" y="32" text-anchor="end" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" letter-spacing="3" fill="rgb(184,85,46)">CITED OUTCOME</text>
					<g font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="rgb(14,17,22)">
						<g transform="translate(48 80)"><rect width="240" height="40" fill="rgb(250,250,247)" stroke="rgb(14,17,22)" stroke-opacity="0.15" rx="4" /><text x="16" y="26" font-weight="600">Google Business Profile</text></g>
						<g transform="translate(48 132)"><rect width="240" height="40" fill="rgb(250,250,247)" stroke="rgb(14,17,22)" stroke-opacity="0.15" rx="4" /><text x="16" y="26" font-weight="600">Menu schema + diet tags</text></g>
						<g transform="translate(48 184)"><rect width="240" height="40" fill="rgb(250,250,247)" stroke="rgb(14,17,22)" stroke-opacity="0.15" rx="4" /><text x="16" y="26" font-weight="600">Vibe and occasion content</text></g>
						<g transform="translate(48 236)"><rect width="240" height="40" fill="rgb(250,250,247)" stroke="rgb(14,17,22)" stroke-opacity="0.15" rx="4" /><text x="16" y="26" font-weight="600">Recent review velocity</text></g>
					</g>
					<g stroke="rgb(14,17,22)" stroke-opacity="0.2" fill="none">
						<path d="M 288 100 C 360 100, 380 178, 440 178" /><path d="M 288 152 C 360 152, 380 178, 440 178" /><path d="M 288 204 C 360 204, 380 178, 440 178" /><path d="M 288 256 C 360 256, 380 178, 440 178" />
					</g>
					<g transform="translate(440 130)">
						<rect width="200" height="100" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" rx="6" />
						<text x="100" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" letter-spacing="2" fill="rgb(250,250,247)" fill-opacity="0.6">AI ENGINES</text>
						<text x="100" y="68" text-anchor="middle" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="rgb(250,250,247)">ChatGPT · Perplexity</text>
						<text x="100" y="86" text-anchor="middle" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="rgb(250,250,247)">AI Overviews · Maps</text>
					</g>
					<g stroke="rgb(184,85,46)" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round">
						<path d="M 640 180 C 700 180, 760 180, 820 180" />
						<polyline points="810,174 820,180 810,186" />
					</g>
					<g transform="translate(820 110)">
						<rect width="212" height="140" fill="rgb(250,250,247)" stroke="rgb(184,85,46)" stroke-width="1.5" rx="6" />
						<circle cx="32" cy="38" r="18" fill="rgb(184,85,46)" />
						<text x="32" y="44" text-anchor="middle" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="rgb(250,250,247)">01</text>
						<text x="62" y="36" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="rgb(14,17,22)">Best brunch</text>
						<text x="62" y="54" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" fill-opacity="0.6">cited in Brooklyn</text>
						<rect x="20" y="76" width="172" height="6" rx="1" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" fill-opacity="0.75" />
						<rect x="20" y="88" width="140" height="4" rx="1" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" fill-opacity="0.35" />
						<rect x="20" y="98" width="156" height="4" rx="1" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" fill-opacity="0.35" />
						<rect x="20" y="108" width="120" height="4" rx="1" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" fill-opacity="0.35" />
					</g>
					<text id="svc-figure-caption" x="540" y="340" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Figtree, system-ui, sans-serif" font-style="italic" font-size="13" fill="rgb(14,17,22)" fill-opacity="0.7">Diners describe restaurants in vibes. AI matches vibes to restaurants that describe themselves that way.</text>
				</svg>
			</figure>

			<section class="svc-section">
				<h2>The challenge: AI is the new dining concierge</h2>
				<p>
					Restaurant search behavior has fully moved into conversational, AI-mediated queries. The
					businesses that get cited are the ones with rich structured menus, well-managed reviews, and
					content that maps to how people actually describe a craving.
				</p>
				<div class="outcomes">
					<div class="outcome"><strong>"Best of" queries get summarized</strong><span>Google AI Overviews now answer "best tacos in Austin" or "best date-night restaurant in Chicago" with a short list. Restaurants outside that list get no consideration set, no matter how good they are.</span></div>
					<div class="outcome"><strong>Diners ask AI for vibes</strong><span>People describe restaurants in feelings now: "cozy," "good for a first date," "loud but fun." AI systems match those queries to restaurant content, not just categories. If your site does not describe your vibe, you are not in the answer.</span></div>
					<div class="outcome"><strong>Menu schema is now table stakes</strong><span>Restaurants without structured menu data are invisible to AI systems looking for "where can I get gluten-free pizza in the West Loop." Schema is no longer optional.</span></div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="svc-section">
				<h2>What we do for restaurants</h2>
				<p>Three services built for the way AI search evaluates and surfaces dining content.</p>
				<ol class="svc-list">
					<li>
						<div class="svc-row">
							<span class="svc-row-num">01</span>
							<div>
								<h3>Restaurant Visibility Audit</h3>
								<p>A complete review of how your restaurant appears across Google, the map pack, AI Overviews, ChatGPT, and Perplexity for the searches that actually drive reservations and walk-ins. You get a prioritized roadmap, with the quickest wins called out.</p>
								<ul><li>Google Business Profile audit</li><li>AI citation analysis for cuisine and category</li><li>Menu and dietary tag <a href="/seo/schema-markup/">schema</a> review</li><li>Review velocity and sentiment review</li><li>Competitor positioning</li></ul>
							</div>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li>
						<div class="svc-row">
							<span class="svc-row-num">02</span>
							<div>
								<h3>Menu and Discovery Optimization</h3>
								<p>Implementation work that turns your restaurant into a richly structured, AI-friendly resource. The schema, content, and review systems that get you surfaced when people ask AI for a recommendation.</p>
								<ul><li>Menu <a href="/seo/schema-markup/">schema</a> with dietary tags and prices</li><li>Restaurant and LocalBusiness schema</li><li>Cuisine, occasion, and vibe content</li><li>Review generation and response systems</li><li>Multi-location consistency for groups</li></ul>
							</div>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li>
						<div class="svc-row">
							<span class="svc-row-num">03</span>
							<div>
								<h3>Ongoing Restaurant AI SEO</h3>
								<p>Monthly support combining seasonal menu updates, event content, technical SEO, Google Business Profile management, and AI citation monitoring so you stay the cited restaurant for your cuisine and city.</p>
								<ul><li>Seasonal menu and event content</li><li>Google Business Profile management</li><li>Review velocity and response systems</li><li>AI citation monitoring and monthly reporting</li></ul>
							</div>
						</div>
					</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section class="svc-section">
				<h2>Why restaurants need AI SEO now</h2>
				<p>Hospitality margins are tight. Filling tables on a Tuesday is the difference between a great month and a bad one. AI search visibility is the cheapest, most durable lever you have.</p>
				<div class="outcomes">
					<div class="outcome"><strong>Walk-ins are now AI-mediated</strong><span>"Where should we eat?" is now an AI conversation, not a Google search. The restaurant cited gets the cover.</span></div>
					<div class="outcome"><strong>Reviews drive everything</strong><span>Recent five-star reviews now influence local pack rankings, Google Business Profile prominence, and AI recommendations. The compounding effect is real.</span></div>
					<div class="outcome"><strong>Structured menus get rewarded</strong><span>Restaurants with proper menu schema and dietary tags get pulled into AI answers for niche queries that competitors miss entirely.</span></div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="svc-section" id="quote">
				<h2>Get a quote for restaurant SEO</h2>
				<p>Book a free 15-minute strategy call or send a quote request below. We respond within one business day.</p>
				<div class="contact-block">
					<div class="contact-card">
						<h3>Book a strategy call</h3>
						<p>We will review your restaurant's current visibility, your cuisine and category, and where AI SEO can have the biggest impact on covers and revenue.</p>
						<a class="svc-btn svc-btn-primary" href={CALENDLY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Calendly &rarr;</a>
					</div>
					<div class="contact-card">
						<h3 id="quote-form-heading">Request a quote by form</h3>
						<p>Tell us about your restaurant, cuisine, and goals, and we will reply with a tailored plan.</p>
						<form class="contact-form" id="quote-form" aria-labelledby="quote-form-heading">
							<input type="hidden" name="access_key" value={WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY} />
							<input type="hidden" name="subject" value="Restaurant SEO quote request from aiseoshift.com" />
							<input type="hidden" name="from_name" value="AISEOShift Restaurant SEO Quote Form" />
							<input type="checkbox" name="botcheck" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />
							<label for="q-name">Name <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
							<input id="q-name" type="text" name="name" required aria-required="true" autocomplete="name" />
							<label for="q-email">Email <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
							<input id="q-email" type="email" name="email" required aria-required="true" autocomplete="email" />
							<label for="q-company">Restaurant / website</label>
							<input id="q-company" type="text" name="company" autocomplete="organization" />
							<label for="q-service">Service interested in <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
							<select id="q-service" name="service" required aria-required="true">
								<option value="">Select a service…</option>
								<option value="Restaurant Visibility Audit">Restaurant Visibility Audit</option>
								<option value="Menu and Discovery Optimization">Menu and Discovery Optimization</option>
								<option value="Ongoing Restaurant AI SEO">Ongoing Restaurant AI SEO</option>
								<option value="Not sure yet">Not sure yet</option>
							</select>
							<label for="q-message">Tell us about your restaurant and goals <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
							<textarea id="q-message" name="message" required aria-required="true" placeholder="Cuisine type, number of locations, city, and what you are trying to achieve."></textarea>
							<button type="submit">Send quote request</button>
							<div class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
						</form>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="svc-section">
				<h2>Restaurant SEO FAQs</h2>
				<ul class="faq-list">
					<li>
						<h3>How much does SEO cost for restaurants?</h3>
						<p>Restaurant SEO typically ranges from $1,000 to $5,000 per month depending on the number of locations, market size, and goals. Single-location independents need less than multi-location groups. Many restaurants get significant lift from Google Business Profile optimization and review systems alone, before any content work.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>How long does restaurant SEO take to work?</h3>
						<p>Restaurants often see results faster than most local businesses, sometimes within four to eight weeks. The reason is that Google Business Profile fixes, menu schema, and review velocity push results quickly. Brand and category searches like "best Italian restaurant in Brooklyn" take longer in competitive metros.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>Do restaurants need AI SEO?</h3>
						<p>Yes. Diners now ask ChatGPT and Perplexity for restaurant recommendations, dietary-restriction-friendly spots, and birthday-worthy patios. Google AI Overviews summarize "best brunch in Austin" instantly. If your restaurant is not surfaced in those <a href="/ai-seo-shift/">AI answers</a>, you lose covers to restaurants that are.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>What is menu schema and does it matter?</h3>
						<p>Menu <a href="/seo/schema-markup/">schema</a> (Schema.org Menu) is structured data that tells search engines exactly what dishes you serve, with prices, allergen information, and dietary tags. Properly marked-up menus appear in rich results, get pulled into AI-generated recommendations, and are favored by both Google and AI systems when answering food queries.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>How important are reviews for restaurant SEO?</h3>
						<p>Reviews are arguably more important for restaurants than any other vertical. They drive Google Business Profile prominence, feed AI recommendation engines, influence map pack rankings, and shape brand trust. Recent positive reviews matter more than older ones, so review velocity and freshness are now ranking factors in their own right.</p>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
